# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "**Not every subject is a compose project.** Discourse is built by its own `./launcher rebuild` ([handlers/stack_host.yml](../../../web-app-discourse/handlers/stack_host.yml)) and runs as a plain container with no compose label. The drill treats such a container as a subject whenever it mounts a volume this generation backed up: it is stopped with everything else and started again at the end, and its return is asserted like any other. Left running it would take an `rsync --delete` into its live data directory, and the chain's consumer check — which reads compose labels — would not see it, so the dump replay would race it exactly like the zammad failure this whole change came from."
msgstr "**Hindi lahat ng paksa ay isang proyektong kinatha.** Ang komunikasyon ay itinatayo sa ganang sarili nito `./launcher rebuild` ([handlers/stack_host.yml](../../../web-app-discourse/handlers/stack_host.yml)) at tumatakbo bilang isang payak na lalagyan na walang tatak ng katha. Ginagamot ng barena ang isang sisidlan na gaya ng isang paksa kailanma't ito'y tataas sa isang tomo na itinataguyod ng salinlahing ito: ito'y pinahihinto sa lahat ng iba pang bagay at muling sinisimulan sa dulo, at ang pagbabalik nito ay iginigiit na gaya ng iba. Ang pag - iiwan dito ay mangangailangan ng isang bagay `rsync --delete` sa live data directory nito, at hindi ito makikita ng tseke ng chain — na kababasahan ng mga etiketa ng katha, kaya ito'y kalahiin ng dump na gaya ng kabiguan ng zammad sa buong pagbabagong ito."

