# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Daniel Kahneman's split names the shape. The models behind the gateway are System II: slow, general, token-generating. What is missing is System I: fast, typed, no generation, deciding which System II model answers. TypeSafe released [Jev](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jev_(AI_model)) on 2026-09-15 as a model of exactly that kind, and [jev-router](https://github.com/prismhq/jev-router) wires one into LiteLLM as a pre-call hook. This requirement takes that shape and keeps the decision deterministic; decision 8 records why."
msgstr "Sa split na pangalan ni Daniel Kahneman ang hugis. Ang mga modelo sa likod ng tarangkahan ay System II: mabagal, pangkalahatan, token-generating. Ang kulang ay ang System I: mabilis, minakinilya, walang henerasyon, na nagpapasiya kung aling System II ang sasagot. Talaan ng mga Nilalaman [Jev](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jev_(AI_model)) patuloy 2026-09-15 bilang isang huwaran ng ganiyang uri, at [jev-router](https://github.com/prismhq/jev-router) Ikabit ang isa sa LitLM bilang pre-cal call hook. Ang kahilingang ito ay nagkakaroon ng ganiyang hugis at pinananatiling deterministiko ang pasiya; pasiya 8 ang dahilan."

