# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Files produced by the containerized runner (e.g. `__pycache__/*.pyc` under [`tests/`](tests/), build artefacts) are often owned by `nobody` or another in-container UID and cannot be removed from the host. When a host-level `rm`/`chmod`/edit fails with `Permission denied` on such paths, agents MUST run the cleanup via `make compose-exec` (see [compose.yml](compose.yml); the repo is mounted at `/opt/src/infinito`) and MUST NOT ask the operator which path to take."
msgstr "Mga talaksang ginawa ng mananakbo ng containerized (e.g. `__pycache__/*.pyc` sa ilalim [`tests/`](tests/), gumawa ng mga artefact) ay kadalasang pag - aari ng `nobody` o iba pang in-container na UID at hindi matanggal sa host. Kapag may host-level `rm`/`chmod`/edit ay bigo sa `Permission denied` sa gayong mga landas, pinangangasiwaan ng mga ahenteng MUST ang paglilinis `make compose-exec` (tingnan [compose.yml](compose.yml); ang repo ay nakakabit sa `/opt/src/infinito`) at HINDI mo tanungin ang opereytor kung anong landas ang dapat tahakin."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Files that fail to read (permission errors, non-UTF-8) are silently skipped — that matches the prior caller behaviour of wrapping ``open().read()`` in a bare ``try/except Exception: continue``."
msgstr "Mga talaksan na hindi nababasa (error sa pahintulot, non-UTF-8) ay tahimik na hindi ginagamit — na katugma ng dating tawag na gawi ng pambalot ``open().read()`` sa labas ``try/except Exception: continue``."

