# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "It hooks `http_api_curl` rather than `http_request_args` because the args array cannot express a proxy: WordPress core's `WP_HTTP_Proxy` hardcodes `CURLPROXY_HTTP`, so SOCKS5 is reachable only on the raw cURL handle. Without it, libcurl refuses an `.onion` host at name resolution under [RFC 7686](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7686) — before `/etc/hosts`, `extra_hosts` or DNS is consulted — and the token exchange fails with cURL error 6, which WordPress surfaces as `wp-login.php?login-error=http_request_failed`."
msgstr "Ito'y mga kawit `http_api_curl` sa halip na `http_request_args` sapagkat ang args args ar ay hindi makapagpahayag ng proxy: WordPress core's `WP_HTTP_Proxy` hardcodes `CURLPROXY_HTTP`, kaya mga SOCK5 ay maaabot lamang sa hilaw na hawakan ng cURL. Kung wala ito, ang libcurl ay tumatanggi `.onion` na may pangalang resolusyon sa ilalim ng [RFC 7686](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7686) — bago `/etc/hosts`, `extra_hosts` o DNS ay isinasangguni — at ang bahagyang pagpapalit ay nabibigo sa pagkakamali ng UL 6, na WordPress ng mga bagay gaya ng `wp-login.php?login-error=http_request_failed`."

