# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The classic failure shape (`DNS [OK]`, `TCP [OK]`, `TLS [FAIL] TimeoutError after 8s`) is an __MTU mismatch__, not a TLS-layer bug. Small packets (TCP-SYN, DNS replies) survive; the larger TLS-ServerHello with the certificate chain is dropped silently because the path MTU is below the bridge MTU and ICMP-needs-frag is filtered upstream. When `auth.docker.io` is OK but `ghcr.io` / `registry-1.docker.io` time out, the chain-length difference between hosts (Cloudflare-fronted ≈ small chain, GitHub/AWS ≈ large chain) confirms MTU as the cause rather than a blanket TLS block."
msgstr "Ang klasikong hugis ng kabiguan (`DNS [OK]`, `TCP [OK]`, `TLS [FAIL] TimeoutError after 8s`) ay isang mismatch__, hindi isang bug ng TLS-layer. Maliliit na pakete (Mga Sagot ng TCP-SYN, DNS) Nakaligtas; ang mas malaking TLS-Striever Hello na may sertipikong kadena ay tahimik na ibinababa dahil ang landas na MTU ay nasa ibaba ng tulay na MTU at ICMP-needs-frag ay sinasala pasalungat. Kailan `auth.docker.io` ay OK ngunit `ghcr.io` / `registry-1.docker.io` Paglabas, ang kadena-habang pagkakaiba ng mga host (Cloudflare-fronted ≈ maliit na chain, GitHub/AWS ≈ malaking chain) Pinatutunayan ang MTU bilang sanhi sa halip na bloke ng kumot na TLS."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "The classification of \"runnable\" and \"incompatible\" is computed by the Jinja filter `nextcloud_install_status` defined in [roles/web-app-nextcloud/filter_plugins/nextcloud_install.py](../../../filter_plugins/nextcloud_install.py). The filter inspects `rc`, `stdout`, and `stderr` from the OCC call and returns flags that drive `until`, `failed_when`, and `when`."
msgstr "Ang klasipikasyon ng \"runnable\" at \"incompatible\" ay nahabi ng filter ng Jinja `nextcloud_install_status` binigyang - katuturan sa [roles/web-app-nextcloud/filter_plugins/nextcloud_install.py](../../../filter_plugins/nextcloud_install.py). Sinusuri ng filter `rc`, `stdout`, at `stderr` mula sa OCC tumawag at bumalik ng mga bandila na nagpapatakbo `until`, `failed_when`, at `when`."

