# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "Today most role specs gate their authenticated scenarios on `oidc` only, even when the role's `meta/services.yml` also declares `ldap.enabled` and a dedicated LDAP auth plugin / driver is wired in. Consequence: a deploy with `disable=oidc` (LDAP-only mode) makes every authenticated scenario `skip`, leaving the LDAP path untested. The matrix-deploy variant lists in `meta/variants.yml` typically include an LDAP-only variant exactly to exercise that branch (see e.g. [web-app-opencloud/meta/variants.yml](../../roles/web-app-opencloud/meta/variants.yml) where variant 1 sets `ldap.enabled: true` with `oidc.enabled: false`), but the corresponding spec scenario does not exist yet."
msgstr "Karamihan ng mga specty specs sa ngayon ay nasa tapat ng kanilang mapananaligang mga senaryo `oidc` Kahit kailan lang `meta/services.yml` sabi rin ng `ldap.enabled` at isang dedikadong LDAP auth plagin / tsuper ang nakatali sa kawad. Katanungan: paggamit ng `disable=oidc` (LDAP-lamang mode) ang bawat tunay na tagpo `skip`, pag-iwan sa landas ng LDAP nang hindi sinusubok. Ang matrix-deploy variant list sa `meta/variants.yml` Karaniwang kasama ang isang LDAP-lamang na variant na eksaktong mag-eehersisyo sa sangay na iyon (tingnan ang e.g. [web-app-opencloud/meta/variants.yml](../../roles/web-app-opencloud/meta/variants.yml) kung saan naiiba 1 mga set `ldap.enabled: true` kasama `oidc.enabled: false`), ngunit ang katumbas na senaryong spec ay hindi pa umiiral."

