# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "What still blocks it is the transport. `server.py` speaks streamable HTTP upstream: `post_upstream` POSTs JSON-RPC to one URL and reads the reply, optionally SSE-framed. Baserow serves the older HTTP+SSE transport, where the client opens the stream and posts to the endpoint that stream announces — the shape `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` implements for `transport: sse` (\"the stream is the response channel and the endpoint it announces is the request channel\"). Fronting Baserow therefore needs that client transport in the adapter, or evidence that Baserow 2.3.3 also accepts a plain streamable-HTTP POST, which only a running instance can settle. A second consequence is waiting behind it: `web-app-n8n` speaks only `sse`, so it drops out of `allowed_consumers` the moment the surface becomes `streamable_http`."
msgstr "Ang humahadlang pa rin dito ay ang transportasyon. `server.py` HTTP sa tabi ng ilog: `post_upstream` POSTs JSON-RPC sa isang URL at basahin ang tugon, opsyonal na SSE-framed. Pinaglilingkuran ni Baserow ang mas lumang sasakyang HTTP+SE, kung saan binubuksan ng kliyente ang sapa at mga poste sa toppoint na nag - aanunsiyo — ang hugis `roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/contract.py` Mga kagamitan para sa `transport: sse` (\"ang daluyan ng tugon at ang hudyat na ipinahahayag nito ay ang request channel\"). Harap Baserow Kaya kailangan ng kliyenteng iyon na ihatid ang tagabagay, o katibayan na Baserow 2.3.3 Tanggapin din ang payak na streamable-HTTP POST, na tanging isang running compilation lamang ang maaaring malutas. Ang ikalawang resulta ay ang paghihintay sa likod nito: `web-app-n8n` ay nagsasalita lamang `sse`, kaya ito ay bumababa `allowed_consumers` sa sandaling ang ibabaw ay maging `streamable_http`."

