msgstr "Kapag nagawa ng OIDC, sinisira o itinatago mo ang normal na login form sa UI kung ang target na application ay hindi pa nakapagbibigay ng dedikadong pagbabago para sa paggawing iyon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When Playwright coverage is included"
msgstr "Kapag isinama ang Pagsaklaw ng Playwright"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When To Use Which 🎯"
msgstr "Kung Kailan Gagamitin ang Alin 🎯"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `Dockerfile.j2` Is Acceptable 🤔"
msgstr "Kailan `Dockerfile.j2` Kanais - nais 🤔"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When ``svc-net-tor`` is deployed, the node’s ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY`` is the minted ``.onion`` address, so the whole stack (web vhosts, Keycloak SSO, LDAP, CA) resolves onion domains consistently. The Tor daemon runs as a host-network compose sidecar and maps one hidden service to the host OpenResty (``HiddenServicePort 80 -> 127.0.0.1:80``); per-app subdomains (``<app>.<node>.onion``) are routed by the ``Host`` header. TLS is off on the onion side (onion v3 already provides transport encryption + server authentication); apps still receive ``X-Forwarded-Proto: https`` because ``.onion`` is a browser Secure Context."
msgstr "Kailan ``svc-net-tor`` ay ginagamit, ang mga nodeiler ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY`` ay ginawa ``.onion`` address, kaya ang buong salansan (mga web vhost, Keycloak SSO, LDAP, CA) ang mga dako ng sibuyas nang walang pagbabago. Ang Tor daemon ay tumatakbo bilang host-network na platform sidecar at mga mapa isang nakatagong serbisyo sa host OpenResty (``HiddenServicePort 80 -> 127.0.0.1:80``); mga subdomain ng per-app (``<app>.<node>.onion``) ay binabagtas ``Host`` header. Nasa tabi ng sibuyas ang TLS (sibuyas v3 ay nagbibigay na ng encryption + server realation); tumatanggap pa rin ng mga app ``X-Forwarded-Proto: https`` sapagkat ``.onion`` ay isang browser security Context."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When ``svc-net-tor`` is in the deploy, mint (or reuse) the node onion and set ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` in the host_vars."
msgstr "Kailan ``svc-net-tor`` na ginagamit, ang matto (o muling gamitin) ang node sibuyas at set ``applications.svc-net-tor.services.tor.node`` sa loob host_vars."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When ``tor_node`` is set (svc-net-tor deployed) and the URL's host is the ``primary_domain`` or a subdomain of it, swap that suffix for ``tor_node`` and force the ``http`` scheme (onion services are plaintext-only). Anything else — empty inputs, a host not under ``primary_domain``, an unparseable value — is returned unchanged, so the filter is a safe no-op on clearnet."
msgstr "Kailan ``tor_node`` ay nakatakda (svc-net-tor Ginamit) At ang host ng URL ang ``primary_domain`` o isang subdomain nito, palitan ng suffix ``tor_node`` at pilitin ang ``http`` pakana (Ang mga serbisyo ng sibuyas ay simpleng-ext-lamang). . Kahit ano pa — walang laman na mga input, wala ang host ``primary_domain``, isang di-gaanong halaga – ay ibinalik na hindi nagbabago, kaya ang pansala ay isang ligtas na no-op sa maliwanag nanet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When ``version`` is unset (no services value, no override), the lookup returns the bare ``<image>`` (unpinned) and emits a ``display.warning`` so the operator notices the unpinned reference without aborting the play."
msgstr "Kailan ``version`` ay naka-set (walang halaga sa paglilingkod, walang nananaig), ibinabalik ng viewup ang laman ``<image>`` (hindi nakapinta) at naglalabas ng isang ``display.warning`` Kaya napansin ng opereytor ang walang - halong reperensiya nang hindi ipinalalaglag ang dula."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `cli create role` scaffolds a new role, it prompts for `--clients N` and calls `cli contributing network address suggest --clients N --count 1` to fill in `meta/server.yml.networks.local.subnet` automatically. The contributor MAY override the suggestion interactively. See [port.md](port.md) for the matching ports flow."
msgstr "Kailan `cli create role` Isang bagong papel ang ginagampanan nito, ito'y nag - uudyok ng `--clients N` at mga tawag `cli contributing network address suggest --clients N --count 1` upang punan `meta/server.yml.networks.local.subnet` Kusa. Maaaring daigin ng nag - abuloy ang mungkahi nang interaktibo. Tingnan [port.md](port.md) para sa katugmang mga daungan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `cli create role` scaffolds a new role, it prompts for required port categories per service entity and calls `cli contributing network ports suggest --scope <…> --category <…> --count 1` per slot to fill in the entity's `ports` map. The contributor MAY override either suggestion interactively. See [address.md](address.md) for the matching subnet flow."
msgstr "Kailan `cli create role` Isang bagong papel ang ginagampanan nito, ito'y nag - uudyok ng kinakailangang mga kategorya sa daungan sa bawat service entity at mga tawag `cli contributing network ports suggest --scope <…> --category <…> --count 1` bawat slot upang punan ang entity `ports` mapa. Maaaring daigin ng nag - abuloy ang alinman sa mungkahi nang interaktibo. Tingnan [address.md](address.md) para sa katugmang daloy ng subnet."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `container` is given, `log_path` is interpreted as a path INSIDE that container and read via `docker exec tail`. When `container` is None, `log_path` is read directly from the host filesystem."
msgstr "Kailan `container` ay ibinibigay, `log_path` ay binibigyang - kahulugan bilang isang landas na INSIDE sa sisidlang iyon at binabasa sa pamamagitan ng `docker exec tail`. Kapag `container` ay hindi, `log_path` ay tuwirang binabasa mula sa host filesystem."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `default:` is present, the credential generator MUST NOT generate a new value via `algorithm:`. It writes the literal `default:` string verbatim."
msgstr "Kailan `default:` ay naroroon, ang credential generator MUST HINDI ay lumilikha ng isang bagong halaga sa pamamagitan ng `algorithm:`. Isinusulat nito ang literal `default:` string veratim."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `lookup('users', 'administrator').tokens['web-app-matomo']` is empty, `sys-front-inj-matomo` sets `inj_enabled.matomo = false` for the current domain. This prevents the NGINX template from rendering the Matomo body snippet (which would reference `matomo_site_id`) and skips `inject.yml` entirely. The play continues without error."
msgstr "Kailan `lookup('users', 'administrator').tokens['web-app-matomo']` ay walang laman `sys-front-inj-matomo` mga set `inj_enabled.matomo = false` para sa kasalukuyang sakop. Hinahadlangan nito na isalin ng NGINX template ang NGINX Matomo Ispipet sa katawan (kung alin ang tinutukoy `matomo_site_id`) at mga paglukso `inject.yml` Lubusan. Ang dula ay nagpapatuloy nang walang pagkakamali."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `meta/variants.yml` declares variant-specific behaviour (WordPress Multisite, Moodle LDAP-only, …), the spec MAY add scenarios that gate on a variant-specific env var via `test.skip(!process.env.<VARIANT>_ENABLED, \"<reason naming the variant flag>\")`. Variant-gated scenarios MUST surface in the reporter as `skipped` with a reason naming the flag, never as silent no-ops."
msgstr "Kailan `meta/variants.yml` sabi ng variable-specific na pag-uugali (WordPress Multibong, Moodle LDAP-lamang, ...), ang spec ay maaaring magdagdag ng mga senaryo na sa isang variant-specific env var via `test.skip(!process.env.<VARIANT>_ENABLED, \"<reason naming the variant flag>\")`. Variant-gated na mga senaryo MUST na nasa reporter bilang `skipped` na may dahilan sa pagbibigay ng pangalan sa watawat, hindi kailanman tahimik na no-ops."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `services.talk.enabled` is true, Nextcloud Talk MUST use the dedicated `web-svc-coturn` service for STUN and TURN instead of the HPB port exposed by `web-app-nextcloud`."
msgstr "Kailan `services.talk.enabled` ay totoo, Nextcloud UPANG Gamitin ang inialay `web-svc-coturn` serbisyo para sa SSTUN at TURN sa halip ng port ng HPB na ibinunyag ng `web-app-nextcloud`."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When `svc-net-tor` is deployed, the node's `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` is the minted `.onion` address, so the whole stack (web vhosts, Keycloak SSO, LDAP, CA) resolves onion domains consistently. The Tor daemon runs as a host-network compose sidecar and maps one hidden service to the host OpenResty (`HiddenServicePort 80 -> 127.0.0.1:80`); per-app subdomains (`<app>.<node>.onion`) are routed by the `Host` header. TLS is off on the onion side (onion v3 already provides transport encryption + server authentication); apps still receive `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` because `.onion` is a browser Secure Context."
msgstr "Kailan `svc-net-tor` ay ginagamit, ang node's `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` ay ginawa `.onion` address, kaya ang buong salansan (mga web vhost, Keycloak SSO, LDAP, CA) ang mga dako ng sibuyas nang walang pagbabago. Ang Tor daemon ay tumatakbo bilang host-network na platform sidecar at mga mapa isang nakatagong serbisyo sa host OpenResty (`HiddenServicePort 80 -> 127.0.0.1:80`); mga subdomain ng per-app (`<app>.<node>.onion`) ay binabagtas `Host` header. Nasa tabi ng sibuyas ang TLS (sibuyas v3 ay nagbibigay na ng encryption + server realation); tumatanggap pa rin ng mga app `X-Forwarded-Proto: https` sapagkat `.onion` ay isang browser security Context."

