# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When the iteration target is the full matrix (cross-variant coverage matters more than focused-debug speed), the command you run is fixed by your current situation. Do NOT improvise `mode` or `variant=`: find your situation in the table and run exactly that command."
msgstr "Kapag ang target ng tornation ang ganap na matrix (cross-variant coverage mga bagay-bagay higit pa sa nakatutok-debug na bilis), ang utos na tumatakbo ka ay itinatakda ng iyong kasalukuyang kalagayan. Huwag MAGPAKITA `mode` o `variant=`: ilagay ang iyong kalagayan sa mesa at patakbuhin ang utos na iyon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When the log carries the matrix-deploy round/pass markers, the result is segmented (one block of records per variant round + pass). Otherwise a single combined block is returned. Runtime rows are read from the ``ROLES RECAP`` sections only (never ``TASKS RECAP``, whose role-less task rows would double-count); a log without any recap header falls back to reading every profile-shaped line. The recap ``total`` line survives as the ``total`` row so consumers can cross-check the parsed sum. Per-host task results (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` under a ``TASK [role : ...]`` header) accumulate into each record's ``hosts`` field; delegation targets (``[host -> other]``) count for the source host. Raises FileNotFoundError when the log is absent (the caller turns that into a hard failure)."
msgstr "Kapag dinadala ng troso ang matrix-deploy round/pass markers, ang resulta ay segmented (isang bloke ng plaka sa bawat variant round + pass). Kung hindi, ibabalik ang isang pinagsamang block. Binabasa mula sa ``ROLES RECAP`` bahagi lamang (Hindi kailanman ``TASKS RECAP``, na ang mga character-walang task row ay dodoble-count); isang log na walang anumang recap header ay nahuhulog pabalik sa pagbabasa ng bawat profile-shaped line. Ang recap ``total`` Nananatiling buháy ang linya habang ang ``total`` hanay upang ang mga mamimili ay maaaring tumawid-check sa parsed sum. Nagbunga ng Per-host task (``ok:``, ``changed:``, ``skipping:``, ``fatal:``, ``failed:`` sa ilalim ng a ``TASK [role : ...]`` header) magtipon sa bawat rekord ``hosts`` field; mga puntirya ng delegasyon (``[host -> other]``) ang source host. Raises File NotFoundError kapag wala ang troso (Ginagawa iyon ng tumatawag na isang malaking kabiguan)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "When the oauth2-proxy SSO flavor is active, Snipe-IT’s native ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` is enabled via the ``Setting`` model (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). nginx gates ``/login`` through oauth2-proxy/Keycloak and injects the verified ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` header, which Snipe-IT matches against ``users.username`` (the user must pre-exist and be activated — sync them via LDAP) to mint a native ``snipeit_session``. Visitors without a matching activated user silently fall through to the normal login form (no error). The password/LDAP login form stays available as a fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), and the in-app logout is redirected to the central OIDC end-session URL."
msgstr "Kapag ang oauth2-proxy SSO lasa aktibo, Snipe-ITixis katutubo ``loginViaRemoteUser()`` sa pamamagitan ng ``Setting`` modelo (``login_remote_user_enabled``, ``login_remote_user_header_name = HTTP_X_FORWARDED_PREFERRED_USERNAME``). gateways ng nininx ``/login`` hanggang sa oauth2-proxy/Keycloak at itinuturok ang napatunayan ``X-Forwarded-Preferred-Username`` Tagapangulo, na kalaban ng Snipe-IT ``users.username`` (ang gumagamit ay dapat na mag-pre-exist at i-crew — syncled ang mga ito sa pamamagitan ng LDAP) upang gumawa ng isang katutubo ``snipeit_session``. Ang mga bisitang walang katapat na aktibong gumagamit nito ay tahimik na nahuhulog sa normal na anyong login (walang error). Ang password/LDAP login form ay nananatiling magagamit bilang fallback (``login_common_disabled = 0``), at ang in-app logout ay ini-redirect sa gitnang OIDC end-session URL."

