msgstr "[x] Ang bawat MCP server endpoint ay protektado ng OIDC, app-password, bearer-token, terrough-session auth, o isang maliwanag na dokumentadong internasyunal-lamang na eksepsiyon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] Every MCP server role declares an application-scoped `mcp` RBAC role, and each client enforces the corresponding server grant. Open WebUI MAY resolve or create its unpredictable local group identifier by group name and apply `access_grants` through the API, but unscoped `roles: [mcp]`, wrong-application membership, last-group removal, and post-restart reconciliation MUST be fixed and tested as defined by requirement 035. All four hold: `granted_roles` drops an `APPLICATION_SCOPED_ROLES` name declared unscoped (`test_rbac_scoped.py::test_an_unscoped_scoped_role_grants_nothing_anywhere`); a scoped grant reaches only its own application, and another provider's group id does not enable a connection (`test_mcp_tool_server_connections.py`); `reconcile_members` sets a group to exactly the entitled set rather than relying on the claim sync (`test_provision_mcp_grants.py::test_a_group_that_lost_its_last_member_is_emptied`); and the grant travels in `TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS`, so a restart restores it. The declaration itself is held by [test_mcp_server_rbac_role.py](../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_server_rbac_role.py)."
msgstr "[x] Ang bawat papel ng MCP server ay nagpapahayag ng aplikasyon-scoped `mcp` RBAC papel, at ang bawat kliyente ay nagpapatupad ng kaukulang donasyon ng server. Maaaring malutas o likhain ng Open WebUI ang di - mahulaang lokal na grupo nito na nakilala sa pamamagitan ng pangalan ng grupo at kapit `access_grants` sa pamamagitan ng API, ngunit hindi nakopya `roles: [mcp]`, maling-application na miyembro, huling-group na pag-alis, at post-restart pakikipagkasundo MUST ay i-edit at subukan na binigyang kahulugan ng kahilingan 035. Lahat ng apat ay: `granted_roles` ay naghulog ng `APPLICATION_SCOPED_ROLES` Ipinahayag na hindi nakopya ang pangalan (`test_rbac_scoped.py::test_an_unscoped_scoped_role_grants_nothing_anywhere`); ang isang saklaw na kaloob ay nakaaabot lamang sa sarili nitong aplikasyon, at ang isa pang grupo ng provider na id ay hindi nagpapangyari ng koneksyon (`test_mcp_tool_server_connections.py`); `reconcile_members` ay nagtatakda sa isang grupo na eksaktong magtakda ng pinamagatang set sa halip na umasa sa sabay - sabay na pag - aangkin (`test_provision_mcp_grants.py::test_a_group_that_lost_its_last_member_is_emptied`); at ang donasyon ay pumapasok `TOOL_SERVER_CONNECTIONS`, kaya pinanauli ito ng isang restart. Ang deklarasyon mismo ay ginaganap ng [test_mcp_server_rbac_role.py](../../tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_server_rbac_role.py)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] Every MCP server role documents whether calls execute as the requesting user, a service account, or an administrator, and the implementation verifies the real provisioned identity. The lookup named here has since been replaced: `lookup('mcp_credential')` resolves the provider's declared `mcp.credential.owner`, `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_no_administrator_token.py` forbids that owner from being `administrator` and forbids task code from reading `users.administrator.tokens`, and all 24 server roles declare `auth_subject: service_account` against a role-scoped `mcp-<application_id>` account. The deploy-time probe authenticates *as* that owner before asserting the tool contract, so a token belonging to anyone else fails the deploy."
msgstr "[x] Bawat MCP ay may papel na ginagampanan sa mga dokumento kung baga ang mga tawag ay isinasagawa bilang isang humihiling na gagamit, isang service account, o isang administrador, at ang pagpapatupad ay nagpapatunay sa tunay na inilaang pagkakakilanlan. Ang hitsura na ipinangalan dito ay napalitan na: `lookup('mcp_credential')` ang ipinahayag ng tagapaglaan `mcp.credential.owner`, `tests/lint/ansible/services/test_mcp_no_administrator_token.py` Ipinagbabawal sa may - ari na maging `administrator` at ipagbawal ang kodigo ng gawain sa pagbabasa `users.administrator.tokens`, at lahat 24 Ipinahahayag ang papel ng server `auth_subject: service_account` laban sa bahaging-scopted `mcp-<application_id>` ulat. Ang kasalukuyang-time probe realitates *gaya ng* na ang may - ari bago igiit ang kontrata sa kagamitan, kaya ang isang tanda na pag - aari ng sinuman ay hindi naglalagay nito."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] Every bridge that is `true` under `services.matrix.plugins.<bridge>` shows up enabled in the rendered `vars.yml` with the matching MDAD enable-flag (`matrix_mautrix_telegram_enabled: true` etc.), and every bridge that is `false` shows up disabled. Verified by reading the rendered file."
msgstr "[x] Bawat tulay `true` sa ilalim `services.matrix.plugins.<bridge>` ay nagpapangyari sa salin `vars.yml` kasabay ng matching MDAD make-flag (`matrix_mautrix_telegram_enabled: true` Atbp.), at ang bawat tulay `false` ang may kapansanan. Pinalitan sa pamamagitan ng pagbasa sa isinaling talaksan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "[x] Every fixture (sample page, sample image, admin credentials) is created inside the workflow run — no external state, no flaky network dependency."
