msgid "``FILE_ENVIRONMENT`` (default: ``/etc/environment``)"
msgstr "``FILE_ENVIRONMENT`` (default: ``/etc/environment``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``FRAMEWORK``: top-level ``meta/services.yml`` integration keys mapped to the in-axis target entity they wire the role into (the infinito-native, group-gated service flags), distinct from the curated upstream edges;"
msgstr "``FRAMEWORK``: itaas-level ``meta/services.yml`` Pagsasama ng mga key para sa in-axis target entity ay ikinakabit nila ang papel sa (ang mga infinito-native, group-gated service flags), naiiba sa kulot na gilid sa itaas;"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``False`` when the covered variant pins ``services.tor.enabled`` to a literal false, ``True`` otherwise. A reactive Jinja flag counts as capable: it is the role saying \"onion when the node is dark\". Consulting the variant matters -- roles pin the gate ``true`` in variant 0 and ``false`` in the rest, so reading only the base config claims an onion for rounds that deliberately run without one."
msgstr "``False`` kapag natatakpan ang iba't ibang tono ``services.tor.enabled`` sa literal na kasinungalingan, ``True`` Pero hindi. Itinuturing ng isang reactitive Jinja flag na may kakayahan: ito ang bahaging nagsasabi ng \"sibuyas kapag madilim na ang node\". Pagsangguni sa iba't ibang bagay -- ang mga papel na ginagampanan ay nag - iindorso sa tarangkahan ``true`` sa mga pagkakaiba 0 at ``false`` sa natitirang bahagi, kaya ang pagbasa lamang ng base deflict ay nag - aangkin ng isang sibuyas para sa mga bilog na sadyang tumatakbo nang walang isa man."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``GH_TOKEN`` env var"
msgstr "``GH_TOKEN`` env var"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "``GITLAB_ROOT_PASSWORD`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__, from ``GITLAB_INIT_ROOT_PASSWORD`` in ```vars/main.yml`` <./vars/main.yml>`__) belongs to GitLab’s built-in ``root`` account, not to the Keycloak ``administrator`` username the persona signs in with, and no GitLab account is provisioned for ``biber`` at all — the OmniAuth sign-in is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` ang sabi ng tao at ng baseline."

