# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, so deploying this role is what switches the gateway from a weighted score to a System One decision."
msgstr "```svc-ai-litellm`` <../svc-ai-litellm/>`__ publishes one routing alias. When this service is deployed, the gateway’s pre-call hook asks it which of the eligible models should answer, passing the prompt as the state and the surviving aliases as the options of a single ``choice`` question. ``services.litellm.router.strategy`` follows ``services.s1.enabled``, kaya ang paglalagay ng papel na ito ang nagpapabago sa pintuang - daan mula sa mabigat na iskor tungo sa isang iskor System One magpasiya."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` unconditionally."
msgstr "```tasks/01_admin.yml`` <./tasks/01_admin.yml>`__ provisions only the administrator in Shopware’s user table. ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__ pins ``services.sso.flavor: oidc``, so no oauth2-proxy fronts the role and the storefront carries no authenticated surface at all; the Keycloak login provider that ```tasks/setup/oidc.yml`` <./tasks/setup/oidc.yml>`__ configures covers the administration backend alone. ``biber`` therefore has no account in any matrix variant and ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` Walang pasubali."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```tasks/01_setup.yml`` <./tasks/01_setup.yml>`__ seeds only the administrator into Magento’s admin table (``bin/magento setup:install --admin-user``, credentials from ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); ``biber`` reaches the backend solely through the oauth2-proxy declared in ```meta/services.yml`` <./meta/services.yml>`__. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that proxy is absent and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` at tumatakbo sa lahat ng iba't ibang paraan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>`__) drives the same admin journey and skips on the same flag."
msgstr "```tasks/05_administrator.yml`` <./tasks/05_administrator.yml>`__ creates the account with ``tootctl accounts create`` and never sets or captures a password, so ``ADMIN_PASSWORD`` — the Keycloak secret — cannot drive Mastodon’s native ``/auth/sign_in``; ``biber`` has no Mastodon account at all, since the OIDC sign-in (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) is the only path that would create one. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that path is removed, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The SeaweedFS companion scenario (```files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js`` <./files/playwright/test-seaweedfs.js>` ) ang nagpapatakbo sa parehong admin na paglalakbay at paglukso sa parehong bandila."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` and asserts the provider, the base URL and the model, so an unconfigured surface cannot reach a green deploy."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml`` <tasks/utils/ai_gateway.yml>`__ runs after ``update.php``. It includes the shared gateway consumer contract, then reads both globals back out of the running container with ``maintenance/run.php getConfiguration --format=json`` at iginigiit ang tagapaglaan, ang base na URL at ang modelo, kaya ang hindi nakaayos na ibabaw ay hindi maaaring umabot sa berdeng gamit."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, unusable password) plus its own workspace, and binds the endpoint to that pair."
msgstr "```tasks/utils/mcp.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp.yml>`__ creates a dedicated non-superuser owner (``mcp@<canonical-domain>``, hindi magagamit na password) At pati na ang sarili nitong workspace, at talian ang dulo ng pares na iyon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` persona and the baseline assertions run unconditionally."
msgstr "```templates/config.exs.j2`` <./templates/config.exs.j2>`__ wires Keycloak as the only login provider this role configures, and ```tasks/main.yml`` <./tasks/main.yml>`__ creates no Mobilizon account; ``MOBILIZON_INSTANCE_DISABLE_DATABASE_LOGIN`` (```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__) additionally closes the database login whenever LDAP is on. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants neither persona has credentials, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true``. The ``guest`` ang sabi ng tao at ng baseline."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` and runs in every variant."
msgstr "```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__ seeds only the administrator into SuiteCRM (``SUITECRM_ADMIN_USERNAME`` / ``SUITECRM_ADMIN_PASSWORD``); ``biber`` reaches the app through SuiteCRM’s own SAML login against Keycloak, where ``SAML_AUTO_CREATE`` mints the account on first assertion. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants there is no SAML entry point and ``biber`` has no native account, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` for the generic persona journeys (the LDAP spec still signs ``biber`` in from the directory). The ``administrator`` persona keeps its native login via ``ADMIN_NATIVE_PASSWORD`` at tumatakbo sa lahat ng iba't ibang paraan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` in every matrix variant, because the shared persona helper cannot drive this role’s sign-in in any of them. Three independent reasons, each sufficient on its own:"
msgstr "```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true`` and ``PERSONA_ADMINISTRATOR_BLOCKED=true`` Sa bawat matrix variant, dahil ang kabahaging taosong katulong ay hindi mapatakbo ang papel na ito ng mga mentilers sign-in sa alinman sa kanila. Tatlong independiyenteng dahilan, bawat isa'y sapat na sa ganang sarili:"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``adapter``:         immutable source contract of a repository-owned adapter. ``category_allowlist`` suits an upstream that switches whole categories and offers no per-tool filter, where a tool allowlist would be unenforceable; ``mcp_passthrough`` fronts an upstream that already speaks MCP instead of translating REST. ``upstream_path`` names that upstream where it lives on the application's own vhost, so the proxy can hide it: reaching it directly walks past the allowlist the adapter exists to enforce. A provider whose upstream is a separate sidecar declares ``upstream_network`` instead and has nothing to hide there."
msgstr "``adapter``: Hindi mababagong kontrata sa pagkukunan ng isang repost-owned adjuster. ``category_allowlist`` ay lumalapat sa isang pasalungat na ilog na nagreresulta sa buong mga kategorya at hindi nag-aalok ng per-tool filter, kung saan ang isang kasangkapang pinahihintulutan ang list ay hindi maipatutupad; ``mcp_passthrough`` Sa harap ng ilog na nagsasalita na ng MCP sa halip na magsalin ng REST. ``upstream_path`` Mga pangalan na nasa gawing itaas nito kung saan ito nakatira sa mismong vhost ng aplikasyon, kaya maaaring itago ito ng proxy: ang pag - abot dito ay tuwirang lampas sa pinahihintulutang mag - adjust ay umiiral upang ipatupad. Isang tagapaglaan na ang pasalungat ay isang hiwalay na sidecar ang nagpapahayag ``upstream_network`` sa halip ay walang anumang itinatago roon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``aliases``: list of DNS aliases. Default: ``[entity_name]`` for shared_net, ``[]`` for default_net"
msgstr "``aliases``: talaan ng mga alyas ng DNS. Pagkawasak: ``[entity_name]`` para sa shared_net, ``[]`` para sa default_net"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``allowed`` (default ``True``): the file (or dotted-path entry) MAY be present for a role of this type. Set ``allowed: False`` to forbid the file/entry on roles of this type so the lint layer can surface the offence with a precise reason."
msgstr "``allowed`` (default ``True``): ang talaksan (o dold-path entry) Maaaring naroroon ang isang bahagi ng uring ito. Itakda ``allowed: False`` upang ipagbawal ang file/entry sa mga papel ng uring ito kaya ang lint layer ay maaaring magresulta sa paglabag na may tiyak na dahilan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible_facts`` only carries ``docker0`` once the daemon has run, and the daemon config is written before that on a fresh node - facts are gathered at play start, and nothing re-gathers them after the install. Reading the fact alone therefore yields nothing on the very run that has to emit the address, which leaves the inner containers pointed at the clearnet resolver and the DinD DNS check failing on a domain only the node dnsmasq knows."
msgstr "``ansible_facts`` ang nagdadala lamang ``docker0`` Minsang tumakbo na ang daemon, at ang daemon conclusion ay isinulat bago pa man na sa isang bagong node - feals ay tinitipon sa play start, at walang re-publish sa kanila pagkatapos ng install. Kung gayon ang pagbabasa lamang ng katotohanan ay hindi nagbubunga ng anumang bagay sa mismong pagtakbo na kailangang maglabas ng direksiyon, na nag - iiwan sa panloob na mga sisidlan na nakatutok sa tagalutas ng nenete at sa DNS na hindi nakagagawa ng sakop na tanging ang node dnsmasq ang nakaaalam."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default)"
msgstr "``ansible`` (default)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ansible`` (default) wraps `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD runs ~70 upstream sub-roles to deliver Synapse, Element, every supported bridge, Element Call, and Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus pins MDAD by commit, renders an MDAD inventory from ``services.matrix.*`` knobs, and disables MDAD’s bundled Traefik / Postgres / Redis so the central Infinito services back the stack."
msgstr "``ansible`` (default) Mga pambalot `matrix-docker-ansible-deploy <https://github.com/spantaleev/matrix-docker-ansible-deploy>`__ (MDAD). MDAD run ~70 Paahon sa sub-roles upang ihatid ang Synapse, Elemento, bawat suportadong tulay, Elementong Tawag, at Jitsi. Infinito.Nexus Mga pin MDAD sa pamamagitan ng paggawa, isalin ang MDAD imbentaryo mula sa MDAD ``services.matrix.*`` Ang mga umbok, at mga Pinsalang MDADimen ay bumubo ng Traefik / Postgres / Postgres / Redis Kaya't ang sentral na mga serbisyong Infinito ay nagbabalik sa salansanan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` is the public S3 endpoint and is reachable without SSO gating."
msgstr "``api.seaweedfs.s3.*`` ang pampublikong S3 Endpoint at ito ay maaabot nang walang SO gating."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` is read from the play variables unless given as ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` names the block instead of ``ports``, for Discourse's launcher file, whose ``expose:`` list is what becomes ``docker run -p`` there."
msgstr "``application_id`` ay binabasa mula sa play variables malibang ibigay bilang ``application_id=``. ``key='expose'`` Sabihin ang pangalan ng block sa halip na ``ports``, sapagkat Discourse' s launcher file, na ang ``expose:`` listahan ang nagiging ``docker run -p`` doon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``application_id`` of the client doing the discovery."
msgstr "``application_id`` ng kliyenteng gumagawa ng tuklas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Home Assistant scopes the token to the account that minted it. This deployment mints it for the administrator, so a call arrives as the administrator whoever asked the client. Entity exposure still bounds the reach. Getting to the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Ang bahay na Tumutulong ay sumasaklaw ng tanda sa ulat na gumawa nito. Ang paglalagay na ito ang gumagawa nito para sa administrador, kaya dumating ang isang panawagan habang ang administrador na nagtanong sa kliyente. Nililimitahan pa rin ng pagkalantad sa entity ang maaabot. Ang pagtungo sa server ng kagamitan ay nasa mga talent motor ``mcp`` grupo ng RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: Mattermost bounds a call by the account the token belongs to. This deployment mints that personal access token for the administrator account, so calls arrive with that account’s rights whoever asked. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: Ang pinakamahalagang bagay ay naglalagay ng isang tawag sa pamamagitan ng ulat na ito. Ang paglalagay na ito ay gumagawa ng paraan na ang personal na magagamit ay tanda ng kuwenta ng administrador, kaya ang mga tawag ay dumarating na may mga karapatan sa account na iyon na sinuman ay humingi. Ang pag - abot sa server ng kagamitan ay pinahihintulutan sa mga plegiers ``mcp`` grupo ng RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the API token is issued against the administrator account, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering Jenkins."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: ang API Nagpalabas ng tanda laban sa kuwenta ng administrador, kaya ang bawat tawag ay nagdadala ng mga karapatan sa kuwentang iyon saanmang magtanong sa kliyente. Ang pag - abot sa server ng kagamitan ay pinahihintulutan sa mga plegiers ``mcp`` grupo ng RBAC, na isang hiwalay na pagkakaloob mula sa paglalapat Jenkins."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the personal access token is minted against the ``root`` account and stored under the ``administrator`` key, so every call carries that account’s rights no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from administering GitLab."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: ang personal na marka ay ginagawa laban sa ``root`` at nakaimbak sa ilalim ng ``administrator`` Ang susi, kaya't ang bawat tawag ay nagdadala ng mga karapatan sa pag - uulat kahit sino man ang magtanong sa kliyente. Ang pag - abot sa server ng kagamitan ay pinahihintulutan sa mga plegiers ``mcp`` grupo ng RBAC, na isang hiwalay na pagkakaloob mula sa paglalapat GitLab."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: administrator``: the web-service token is issued against the administrator account, so a call carries that account’s rights regardless of who asked the client. The attached functions are read-only, which bounds what those rights can do here. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group."
msgstr "``auth_subject: administrator``: ang web-service token ay inilabas laban sa administrator account, kaya ang isang tawag ay nagdadala ng mga karapatan na accountiks kahit sino ang magtanong sa kliyente. Ang mga kaugnay na tungkulin ay basahin-lamang, na tinatakdaan ang magagawa rito ng mga karapatang iyon. Ang pag - abot sa server ng kagamitan ay pinahihintulutan sa mga plegiers ``mcp`` grupo ng RBAC."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``. A call arrives at Baserow as the endpoint owner regardless of who asked the client, and reaches only the one workspace that account owns. That is the second bound under the adapter’s allowlist, not a substitute for it."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``. Dumating ang tawag Baserow bilang ang may - ari ng endpoint anuman ang magtanong sa kliyente, at marating lamang ang isang lugar ng trabaho na pag - aari ng kompanya. Iyan ang ikalawang tali sa ilalim ng mga adjusterifict, hindi isang kahalili nito."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` RBAC group, which is a separate grant from holding a Nextcloud account."
msgstr "``auth_subject: service_account``: ```tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml`` <./tasks/utils/mcp/token.yml>`__ creates the account ``NEXTCLOUD_MCP_USERNAME`` with ``occ user:add`` if it is missing, mints the app password against that account, and stores it under ``mcp.credential.owner``. Every call carries that account’s rights, not the administrator’s, no matter who asked the client. Reaching the tool server is gated on the role’s ``mcp`` grupo ng RBAC, na isang hiwalay na pagkakaloob mula sa paghawak ng isang Nextcloud ulat."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_subject``:    identity MCP calls execute as. ``user`` and ``oidc`` additionally require a ``delegation`` block, because a rendered deployment bearer is a service account no matter what the metadata claims."
msgstr "``auth_subject``: Kung sino ang MCP ay tinatawag na bitayan. ``user`` at ``oidc`` karagdagang nangangailangan ng a ``delegation`` block, dahil ang isang iginawad na supply bearing ay isang service account anuman ang sinasabi ng metadata."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth_type: bearer`` with the token from the discovery data"
msgstr "``auth_type: bearer`` na may paunawa mula sa natuklasang datos"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auth``:            authentication scheme guarding the endpoint."
msgstr "``auth``: Tunay na plano na nagbabantay sa endpoint."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``auto`` is advisory and never fails the unit — every refusal is logged to the journal as ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, so check there if a host you expect to snapshot does not. A stated ``btrfs``/``zfs`` fails the unit instead, which is the point of stating it. Before every snapshot the launcher also removes the ``.baudolo-*`` leftovers a killed run leaves inside the data root."
msgstr "``auto`` ay isang tagapayo at hindi kailanman nabibigo sa yunit — bawat pagtanggi ay nakatala sa babasahin na gaya ng kung ano ang sinasabi ``baudolo-snapshot: live copy, <reason>``, kaya tingnan mo doon kung ang isang host ay inaasahan mong hindi magpo - photos. Isang pangungusap ``btrfs``/``zfs`` ay nabibigo sa halip, na siyang punto ng pagsasabi nito. Bago ang bawat litrato ay inaalis din ng tagapaglunsad ang ``.baudolo-*`` Ang mga natira ay nag-iiwan ng patay na run run sa loob ng data root."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``backend``: ``cloud`` or ``chezmoi``"
msgstr "``backend``: ``cloud`` o ``chezmoi``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``base_dir`` (string): base directory for CA files"
msgstr "``base_dir`` (string): himpilang directory para sa mga talaksang CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``baudolo-restore --empty`` pre-cleans the schema in one psql session and replays the dump in the next, so a consumer that boots in between recreates the schema and the replay dies on its own ``CREATE TABLE``. Hence the refusal while a consumer is up."
msgstr "``baudolo-restore --empty`` Bago-linisin ang schema sa isang sesyon ng psql at muling i-play ang dump sa susunod, kaya ang isang mamimili na ang mga bota sa pagitan ng reproducts ang schema at ang replay ay namamatay sa sarili nito ``CREATE TABLE``. Kaya, ang pagtanggi habang ang isang mamimili ay up."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bench new-site`` uses the central MariaDB’s ``root`` to create the per-site DB on first deploy."
msgstr "``bench new-site`` gamitin ang gitna MariaDBMga pang - aabuso ``root`` upang likhain ang per-site DB na nasa unang pagpopondo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``biber`` only ever exists inside EspoCRM through OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` personas run in every variant."
msgstr "``biber`` sa loob lamang EspoCRM sa pamamagitan ng OIDC auto-provisioning (``ESPOCRM_CONFIG_OIDC_CREATE_USER=true``, ```templates/env.j2`` <./templates/env.j2>`__); the role itself seeds only the administrator account. In the ``services.sso.enabled: false`` matrix variants that provisioning path is gone and no native ``biber`` user exists, so ```templates/playwright.env.j2`` <./templates/playwright.env.j2>`__ renders ``PERSONA_BIBER_BLOCKED=true``. The ``administrator`` and ``guest`` ang lahat ng iba't ibang uri ng tao."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``bond`` states how tightly a role couples to the service it declares: ``>= 1`` keeps the partner on the same host, ``< 1`` lets it live on its own. The value sits on the consumer's side of the relation, so the pair is directed and the two directions of one pair need not agree."
msgstr "``bond`` ay nagsasabi kung gaano kahigpit ang papel ng mga mag - asawa sa paglilingkod na sinasabi nito: ``>= 1`` At laging kayo'y mangagsipanatili sa isa't isa, ``< 1`` hayaang mabuhay ito sa ganang sarili. Ang halaga ay nasa panig ng mamimili na may kaugnayan, kaya ang pares ay nakadirekta at ang dalawang direksiyon ng isang pares ay hindi kinakailangang magkasundo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **parent** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` apex)"
msgstr "``c.wiki.example.com`` → **magulang** ``wiki.example.com`` (plus ``example.com`` Pinakamalaki)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ca_cert_host`` is where sys-ca-selfsigned provisions the root CA on the host. The container-side bind-mount targets live in the ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) and reach the standalone runtime scripts as env vars and CLI arguments."
msgstr "``ca_cert_host`` ay kung saan sys-ca-selfsigned ang ugat na CA sa punong - abala. Ang mga target ng container-side bond-mount ay nakatira sa ``CA_TRUST`` group_vars SPOT (``inject_cert_container`` / ``inject_wrapper_container``) at maabot ang standalone runtime scripts bilang env vars at mga argumento ng CLI."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``canonical_domain`` is the host of ``canonical_url``, not the configured domain, so both follow the onion substitution a Tor deployment applies. A consumer that compares it against what a page actually renders would otherwise never match on an onion host."
msgstr "``canonical_domain`` ang punong - abala ``canonical_url``, hindi ang nakaayos na nasasakupan, kaya kapuwa ito sumusunod sa panghaliling sibuyas na kapit sa isang Tor depostment. Ang isang mamimili na inihahambing ito sa kung ano ang aktuwal na isinasalin ng isang pahina ay hindi kailanman makapapantay sa isang sibuyas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``central_mariadb_root_password``: The root password for the MariaDB server."
msgstr "``central_mariadb_root_password``: Ang root password para sa MariaDB server."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``cert_host`` (string): host path to Root CA certificate"
msgstr "``cert_host`` (string): daan patungo sa sertipiko ng Root CA"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``classification``:  what this role is in the MCP audit. Required."
msgstr "``classification``: kung ano ang papel na ito sa audit ng MCP. Kailangan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``comments`` is the parsed per-key comment map from default.env (see :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dynamic keys carry their comments via each handler's ``COMMENT`` constant. ``custom.env`` overrides run last (see :func:`apply_custom_env`)."
msgstr "``comments`` ang parsed per-key comment map mula sa default.env (tingnan :func:`utils.env.parser.parse_static_env_with_comments`). Dinamic keys ay nagdadala ng kanilang mga komento sa pamamagitan ng bawat handler's ``COMMENT`` Lagi. ``custom.env`` Ang huling mga panalo (tingnan :func:`apply_custom_env`)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose build`` re-bakes the static output whenever the cloned content changes, so deploys are content-driven without any runtime build step."
msgstr "``compose build`` Ang re-bakes ang output ng static kailanma't ang na-record content ay nagbabago, kaya ang mga deposts ay content-joint na walang runtime gumawa ng hakbang."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` and ``pip.conf.j2`` under ``templates/``, and the shell scripts under ``files/``, belong to the development compose stack, which drives them through `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ and `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. The Ansible deployment reads none of them."
msgstr "``compose.cache-consumer.yml.j2``, ``apt.list.j2``, ``npmrc.j2`` at ``pip.conf.j2`` sa ilalim ``templates/``, at ang mga script ng kabibi sa ilalim ``files/``, kabilang sa salansan ng pag - unlad, na nagpapatakbo sa mga ito `render.py <../../utils/cache/render.py>`__ at `compose.py <../../cli/administration/deploy/development/compose.py>`__. Ang Ansible depostment ay walang mababasa sa mga ito."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` (deprecated)"
msgstr "``compose`` (pinabayaan)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` is the in-repo Docker Compose stack. It remains installable but receives no new features."
msgstr "``compose`` ang in-repo Docker Compose magsalansan. Nananatili itong naka-install ngunit hindi tumatanggap ng bagong mga katangian."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``compose`` or ``swarm`` to pin every image to that track, ``rotate`` to split the images across both."
msgstr "``compose`` o ``swarm`` Upang iayon ang lahat ng larawan sa daang yaon, ``rotate`` upang hatiin ang mga larawan sa magkabilang panig."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``composer install`` failed."
msgstr "``composer install`` ay nabigo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``config.access_grants: []``, administrator-only rather than public"
msgstr "``config.access_grants: []``, administrador-lamang sa halip na publiko"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer_not_allowed`` is a decision and simply narrows the result. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` and ``tools_unenforceable`` mean the provider did authorize this consumer and the connection still cannot be rendered, so they abort the run instead of disappearing quietly: a client that silently ends up with fewer tools than the deployment declared is indistinguishable from one that works."
msgstr "``consumer_not_allowed`` ay isang pasiya at basta pinaiikli ang resulta. ``transport_unsupported``, ``auth_unsupported``, ``endpoint_unreachable`` at ``tools_unenforceable`` ay nangangahulugan na binigyang - karapatan ng tagapaglaan ang mamimiling ito at ang koneksiyon ay hindi pa rin maaaring ibigay, kaya't sila'y nagpapalaglag sa pagtakbo sa halip na umalis nang tahimik: isang kliyente na tahimik na nagwawakas na may kakaunting kagamitan kaysa kung saan ang pangangailangan ay ipinahayag na hindi makikilala ng isa na nagtatrabaho."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``consumer``: optional override"
msgstr "``consumer``: Mga opsyonal na pag - aalis"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``container system prune -a -f`` to remove unused Docker resources."
msgstr "``container system prune -a -f`` upang alisin ang hindi ginagamit na mga yaman ng Docker."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``core`` for every language but the source language, ``docs`` for the languages LibreTranslate supports."
msgstr "``core`` para sa bawat wika maliban sa wikang pinagmulan, ``docs`` para sa mga wika LibreTranslate ay umaalalay."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential_missing`` is the one authorized rejection that does not abort, because a provider deploying later in the same play has not written its secret yet. That exemption ends at the reconciliation stage, which runs once every provider has: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` treats it as fatal there."
msgstr "``credential_missing`` ang isa na awtorisadong tanggihan na hindi nagpapalaglag, sapagkat ang isang tagapaglaan na naglalagay sa dakong huli ng dula ding iyon ay hindi pa nakasulat ang lihim nito. Ang eksemsiyong iyan ay nagtatapos sa yugto ng pakikipagkasundo, na minsang magkaroon ang bawat tagapaglaan: ``assert_authorized_are_renderable(discovery, strict=True)`` ituring ito na nakamamatay roon."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credential``:      which principal the provider authenticates as, and where its secret is read from. Replaces the administrator token path."
msgstr "``credential``: na siyang pangunahing tinitiyak ng tagapaglaan bilang, at kung saan binabasa ang lihim nito. Palitan ang administrador ng bahagyang landas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, sent as ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"
msgstr "``credentials.mcp_bearer``, ipinadala bilang ``Authorization: Bearer <bearer>``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``custom.env`` is the operator's untracked override file; its values win over static defaults AND handler-computed values."
msgstr "``custom.env`` ang hindi sirang talaksang dominasyon ng operator; ang mga halaga nito ay nananalo sa static defaults AND handler-computed na mga halaga."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_name``: The name of the initial database to create."
msgstr "``database_name``: Ang pangalan ng paunang database na nilikha."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_password``: The password for the database user."
msgstr "``database_password``: Ang password para sa gumagamit ng database."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``database_username``: The username for the database user."
msgstr "``database_username``: Ang username para sa gumagamit ng database."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``days`` (int): certificate validity"
msgstr "``days`` (int): sertipiko ng sertipiko"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``default-address-pools`` is where docker takes that address from, so the declaration answers before the daemon exists and answers identically afterwards. That also keeps daemon.json byte-identical across passes, which the fact-derived value could not: it appeared only from the second run on and restarted the container runtime under a live stack."
msgstr "``default-address-pools`` ay kung saan kinukuha ng tagadaong ang address na iyon mula sa, kaya ang deklarasyon ay sumasagot bago ang daemon ay umiiral at ang mga sagot ay magkatulad pagkatapos. Nananatili rin iyan daemon.json byte-identical cross passes, na ang fact-derived na halaga ay hindi maaaring: ito ay lumitaw lamang mula sa ikalawang run on at muling ini-record ang container runtime sa ilalim ng live na salansan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``delegation``:      recorded proof, at one exact upstream version, that per-user token acquisition, refresh, audience binding and revocation exist."
msgstr "``delegation``: naitalang patotoo, sa isang eksaktong bersiyon sa itaas ng ilog, na ang per-user token na pagkakamit, pagreresulta, mga manonood na nagtatali at nagpapawalang bisa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``deployment`` restricts to roles present anywhere in ``groups``, which is what a container-network consumer can actually reach; ``all`` returns every declaring role, deployed or not."
msgstr "``deployment`` mga limitasyon sa mga papel na nasa lahat ng dako ``groups``, na siyang maaaring aktuwal na maabot ng isang mamimili ng container-network; ``all`` ay nagbibigay ng lahat ng bahagi, ginagamit man o hindi."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dest``: destination path (required for ``cloud``)"
msgstr "``dest``: paroroonan (kailangan ``cloud``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``direction``:       whether the role exposes MCP, consumes it, or both."
msgstr "``direction``: Inilalantad man ng papel na ito ang MCP, inuubos ito, o kapuwa."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``discourse``: the WP->Discourse post round-trip scenario. Disabling Discourse skips it; front-page reachability and CSP baselines stay active."
msgstr "``discourse``: ang WP->Discourse post round-trip scene. Paghiwalay Discourse Nilalampasan ito; nananatiling aktibo ang front-pahinang accessable at CSP baselines."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``docker_name``    the explicit ``name:`` field (alias for ``name``"
msgstr "``docker_name`` lantaran ``name:`` larangan (alyas para sa ``name``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``domains``: canonical and alias domains"
msgstr "``domains``: kanonikal at alyas na mga sakop"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): run ``doli pull`` after adding mappings"
msgstr "``dotlinker_apply`` (default: ``true``): tumakbo ``doli pull`` pagkatapos magdagdag ng mga mapa"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_cli_name`` (default: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_config_path`` (default: ``~/.config/dotlinker/config.yaml``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"
msgstr "``dotlinker_package_name`` (default: ``doli``)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): pass ``--replace`` to ``doli add``"
msgstr "``dotlinker_replace`` (default: ``true``): lumipas ``--replace`` hanggang sa ``doli add``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dotlinker_user`` (required): user to run ``doli`` as"
msgstr "``dotlinker_user`` (kailangan): tumatakbo ``doli`` gaya ng"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` and ``dsk-gnt-pi`` carry no entry in that map. Cursor is a full editor rather than an extension, and neither vendor publishes an extension on Open VSX, so there is nothing to install into Code for them. Both agents are used from their own binary."
msgstr "``dsk-gnt-cursor`` at ``dsk-gnt-pi`` ay walang ipinapasok sa mapa. Ang Cursor ay isang ganap na editor sa halip na isang extension, at ni ang nagtitinda ay naglalathala ng isang extension sa Open VSX, kaya walang mai-install Code para sa kanila. Ang parehong agent ay ginagamit mula sa kanilang sariling binaryo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enabled`` (bool)"
msgstr "``enabled`` (bool)"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``endpoint``:        connection metadata for clients (server roles only)."
msgstr "``endpoint``: koneksyon metadata para sa mga kliyente (papel ng server lamang)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``enforced`` onions every capable row, ``disabled`` none, ``exclusive`` drops the rows that cannot take one, ``auto`` rotates."
msgstr "``enforced`` sibuyas bawat may kakayahang hanay, ``disabled`` wala, ``exclusive`` ang mga hanay na hindi kayang kunin, ``auto`` Umiikot."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries_only=true`` returns those strings as a list instead of the rendered block, for a container that is not described by a compose file at all: ``web-app-discourse`` is built by discourse_docker's ``launcher``, whose only argument surface is ``docker_args:`` in its ``app.yml``, so it needs ``--add-host=<entry>`` lines."
msgstr "``entries_only=true`` ibalik ang mga kuwerdas na iyon bilang isang talaan sa halip na ang isinaling bloke, para sa isang sisidlan na hindi inilarawan ng isang talaksan ng katha: ``web-app-discourse`` ay itinatayo ng discourse_docker' ``launcher``, na ang tanging pagtatalo ay ang umiiral ``docker_args:`` sa loob nito ``app.yml``, kaya kailangan ``--add-host=<entry>`` linya."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entries`` is a list of dotted-path facts about the file's content. Each entry carries the same ``mandatory`` and ``allowed`` semantics described above and adds a ``marker`` flag (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` declares the path as the type marker for the surrounding type entry. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` walks every ``marker: True`` entry; each marker that resolves to a non-empty value in the role's file adds the surrounding type to the role's type set. ``application_id`` for ``application`` and ``system_service_id`` for ``system-service`` are the canonical markers."
msgstr "``entries`` ay isang talaan ng down-path na mga katotohanan tungkol sa nilalaman ng talaksan. Bawat pasukan ay may pare - parehong karga ``mandatory`` at ``allowed`` Mga semantik na inilarawan sa itaas at nagdaragdag ng isang ``marker`` bandila (default ``False``): ``marker: True`` ang sabi ng daan bilang type marker para sa nakapaligid na pagpasok ng tipo ng titik. :func:`utils.roles.type.get_role_types` naglalakad bawat isa ``marker: True`` Ang pagpasok; ang bawat marker na nagreresulta sa hindi-walang halaga sa talaksang papel ay nagdaragdag ng nakapaligid na tipo sa set ng papel. ``application_id`` para sa ``application`` at ``system_service_id`` para sa ``system-service`` ang kanonikal na mga palatandaan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` declares a ``run-name:`` that interpolates the dispatch inputs. Once a run has started, that title is the only record of them: the REST API answers ``inputs: null`` for a workflow_dispatch run. Anything that wants to know what a run was dispatched with therefore parses the title — and parsing it against a hand-copied format would drift the moment the workflow changes, silently and without a failing test."
msgstr "``entry-manual-steer.yml`` sabi ng isang ``run-name:`` na nag - uugnay sa pahatid na mga input. Minsang magsimula ang pagtakbo, ang titulong iyan ang tanging rekord nila: ang REST API sagot ``inputs: null`` para sa a workflow_dispatch takbo. Anumang bagay na gustong malaman kung ano ang pinadala ng isang pagtakbo ay nag-parse samakatuwid ng pamagat — at ang pag-spink nito sa isang hand-copied formation ay magpapatangay sa sandaling ang workflow ay magbago, tahimik at walang bumabagsak na pagsubok."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ephemeral`` publishes the container port on a host port docker picks, for a service addressed only through the compose network."
msgstr "``ephemeral`` Ilalathala ang port ng container sa isang port pick pick ng host, para sa serbisyo na naka-release lamang sa pamamagitan ng hreform network."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposed`` is an explicit per-service opt-in (default false) that makes the service reachable over the node onion: its port gets a dedicated ``HiddenServicePort``. Because ``applications`` is the variant-merged config (base ``meta/services.yml`` deep-merged with the round's ``meta/variants.yml`` override), a service is forwarded only in the variant/config where it sets ``exposed: true`` — which is exactly what lets the two DB variants be tested over Tor (v0 exposed -> reachable, v1 not -> refused)."
msgstr "``exposed`` ay maliwanag na per-service opt-in (sirang default) na nagpapangyaring maabot ng serbisyo ang node sibuyas: ang daungan nito ay nakakakuha ng isang inialay ``HiddenServicePort``. Sapagkat ``applications`` ang variant-merged na pagkaayos (himpilan ``meta/services.yml`` Pang-ilalim na may round's ``meta/variants.yml`` dominante), isang serbisyo ay pasulong lamang sa variant/config kung saan ito nakalagay ``exposed: true`` — na siyang dahilan kung bakit ang dalawang DB variant ay sinusubok sa ibabaw ng Tor (v0 nakalantad -> maaabot, v1 hindi -> ang tumanggi)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``exposure``:        who may reach the endpoint."
msgstr "``exposure``: sino ang maaaring umabot sa dulo."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``extra_hosts=``, whatever the call site needs on top: a peer's overlay VIP, or a partner service reachable only on the host."
msgstr "``extra_hosts=``, anuman ang kailangan sa itaas ng lugar na pinagtawagan: isang nakabalot na VIP ng isang kasama, o isang paglilingkod ng kapareha na maaabot lamang sa punong - abala."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``false`` while MCP servers are discovered"
msgstr "``false`` samantalang natutuklasan ang mga server ng MCP"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``family`` is the ``os_family`` ansible reports for the host. Callers that have facts (the action plugin) pass it, so distributions outside the CI matrix - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - still resolve through their family. Callers without facts (lints, the availability test) omit it and the family is derived from :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, which only covers the default matrix."
msgstr "``family`` ang siyang ``os_family`` Di - maipaliwanag na mga ulat para sa punong - abala. Mga tumatawag na may katotohanan (ng aksiyon) Dadaan ito, kaya ang mga distribusyon sa labas ng CI Mutant - Manjaro, Mint, Rocky - ay pa rin na nalulutas sa pamamagitan ng kanilang pamilya. Mga Tawag na walang katotohanan (Mga linta, ang makukuhang pagsubok) Alisin ito at ang pamilya ay galing sa :data:`DISTRO_FAMILY`, na sumasaklaw lamang sa default matrix."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` serves the filer web UI behind an admin-only oauth2-proxy."
msgstr "``filer.seaweedfs.s3.*`` Pinaglilingkuran ang filer web UI sa likod ng admin-lamang oauth2-proxy."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (run on the deploy host) completes the first-run wizard (seeds the break-glass admin), installs both plugins via Jellyfin’s own ``/Packages`` installer, writes the plugin configs, and restarts."
msgstr "``files/configure-auth.sh`` (tumatakbo sa kasalukuyang host) tapos ang unang-run magic (buto ng break-glass admin), iluluklok ang dalawang plagin sa pamamagitan ng JellyfinAng mga ’ ``/Packages`` installer, sulat ng plagin conclusions, at mga restart."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/playwright.config.js``: shared Playwright configuration"
msgstr "``files/playwright.config.js``: magkatulad na pagsasaayos ng Playwright"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``files/python/policy.py`` validates it at startup. A contract missing a limit, carrying an empty allowlist, naming a wildcard path or lacking a pinned schema hash is refused before the process serves anything."
msgstr "``files/python/policy.py`` Pinatutunayan ito sa simula. Isang kontratang kulang sa limitasyon, na may dala-dalang walang laman na entlist, na pinangalanan ang isang landas na ligaw o kulang ng pinined schema hash ay tinatanggihan bago ang proseso ay magsilbi ng kahit ano."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flags``: list of flags to AND. Default: ``[enabled, shared]``"
msgstr "``flags``: Listahan ng mga bandila sa ATH. Pagkawasak: ``[enabled, shared]``"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``flavor`` picks the probe shape (see utils/docker/healthcheck/); each flavor brings its own interval, timeout, retries and start_period, and any of those may be overridden next to it. Without a ``flavor`` the entry must carry an explicit ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` selects another entry below ``ports.internal`` for services that expose their probe on a second port."
msgstr "``flavor`` ang numero ng probe (tingnan utils/docker/healthcheck/); ang bawat lasa ay nagdadala ng sarili nitong pagitan, timeout, retries at start_period, at ang alinman sa mga ito ay maaaring nangingibabaw sa tabi nito. Walang ``flavor`` ang entry ay dapat magdala ng maliwanag ``test`` argv. ``port_key`` pumili ng isa pang entry sa ibaba ``ports.internal`` para sa mga serbisyong naglalantad sa kanilang probe sa ikalawang daungan."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``force_regen`` (bool): if true, remove and regenerate key/cert"
msgstr "``force_regen`` (bool): kung totoo, alisin at ibalik ang key/cert"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``forward[A]`` is the list of provider roles that ``A`` directly depends on (services it embeds). ``reverse[B]`` is the list of roles that directly depend on ``B`` (consumers that embed ``B``)."
msgstr "``forward[A]`` ang listahan ng mga papel ng tagapaglaan ``A`` tuwirang depende (mga serbisyo nito). ``reverse[B]`` ang listahan ng mga papel na tuwirang nakadepende sa ``B`` (Mga mamimiling humihibik ``B``)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``galaxy_info.author`` is where a role records who implemented it, so that is where the names are read. A role may credit more than one person, comma separated."
msgstr "``galaxy_info.author`` ay kung saan ang isang papel na ginagampanan nito, upang doon binabasa ang mga pangalan. Ang isang papel ay maaaring magpangalan ng higit sa isang tao, ang comma ay magkahiwalay."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``getent`` honours nsswitch and cannot address a server, so on its own it cannot say which of the resolvers in resolv.conf refused. Where the distro ships a query tool, ask every nameserver directly; where it does not, the per-name verdicts still stand on their own."
msgstr "``getent`` Mga parangal na nsswitch at hindi makakausap ang isang server, kaya sa ganang sarili ay hindi nito masasabi kung alin sa mga nagpapasiya ang nasa resolv.conf Tumanggi. Kung saan ang distro ay nagpapadala ng isang query tool, direktang tanungin ang bawat nameserver; kung saan hindi ito, ang per-name na hatol ay nakatayo pa rin sa kanilang sarili."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` is the single source of truth for host paths. The env layer (utils/env/handlers, exported by scripts/meta/env/load.sh) derives the ``INFINITO_*`` env keys from it; a set env wins so callers can override. When a tool runs outside that layer, e.g. a bare ``subprocess`` that does not inherit the env build, the value is read straight from the group_vars SPOT, so there is still no hardcoded literal default."
msgstr "``group_vars/all/05_paths.yml`` ang nag - iisang pinagmumulan ng katotohanan para sa mga dakong tinutuluyan. Ang env layer (utils/env/handlers, iniluluwas ng scripts/meta/env/load.sh) nakukuha ang ``INFINITO_*`` Nakasingit na mga susi mula rito; isang set env ang panalo upang ang mga tumatawag ay maaaring manaig. Kapag ang isang kasangkapan ay tumakbo sa labas ng suson na iyon, e.g. isang butas ``subprocess`` na hindi nagmamana ng env building, ang halaga ay binabasa nang tuwiran mula sa group_vars SPOT, kaya wala pa ring mahigpit na literal na default."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``host_alias=true``, which pins ``host.docker.internal`` at whatever reaches the host in the effective mode. A container that must talk to a service the host publishes -- msmtp relaying through the swarm ingress on :587, for instance -- needs the alias, and it must not hardcode ``host-gateway`` because that breaks under swarm for the reason below."
msgstr "``host_alias=true``, na siyang mga pink ``host.docker.internal`` anuman ang marating ng punong - abala sa mabisang paraan. Isang lalagyan na dapat makipag - usap sa isang paglilingkod na inilalathala ng punong - abala - ang msmtp na inihahatid sa kuyog ng mga ingreso sa :587, Halimbawa, - kailangan ang alyas, at hindi dapat hardcode ``host-gateway`` sapagkat iyon ay binabasag sa ilalim ng kuyog sa kadahilanang nasa ibaba."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, own network only"
msgstr "``http://giteamcpupstream:8080/mcp``, pagmamay-ari ng network lamang"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` on the shared MCP overlay"
msgstr "``http://nginx:80/webservice/mcp/server.php`` sa pinagsaluhang MCP"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``implementation``:  how the surface is provided, ordered by precedence."
msgstr "``implementation``: kung paano inilalaan ang ibabaw, kung una rito."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``in_container`` exists because one template serves two consumers. The host's /root/.msmtprc is read by the host and loopback is right for it; the copy mounted at /etc/msmtprc is read inside a container, where 127.0.0.1 is that container's own loopback and nothing listens on it. Such a service must also emit ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` so the alias resolves."
msgstr "``in_container`` Ang isang template ay nagsisilbi sa dalawang mamimili. Ang /root/.msmtprc ng host at loopback ay tama para dito; ang kopya na inilagay sa /etc/msmtprc ay binabasa sa loob ng isang container, kung saan ang kopya na nakalagay sa /etc/msmtprc ay binabasa sa loob ng isang lalagyan, kung saan ang kopya nakalagay sa /etc/msmtprc ay binabasa sa loob ng isang lalagyan, kung saan ang isang lalagyan. 127.0.0.1 ang mismong loopback ng container na iyon at walang nakikinig dito. Ang gayong paglilingkod ay dapat ding maglabas ``lookup('container_extra_hosts')`` Kaya nagpasiya ang alyas."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``indent=0`` collapses everything to the left edge - useful when the lookup is rendered into top-level YAML (no service wrapper)."
msgstr "``indent=0`` ang lahat ng bagay sa kaliwang-gamitan kapag ang single-level YAML (walang gamit na pambalot)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``ingress`` (default) emits the short ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` emits the long block with ``mode: host``, which is what an edge role needs in swarm so the client address survives the hop."
msgstr "``ingress`` (default) ay naglalabas ng maikli ``\"host:published:container\"`` string; ``host`` ay naglalabas ng mahabang bloke sa pamamagitan ng ``mode: host``, na siyang mahalagang papel na kailangan sa kuyog upang ang pahayag ng kliyente ay makaligtas sa hop."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal`` (default) reads ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` reuses the published port, for services that cannot remap (STUN/TURN, media relays)."
msgstr "``internal`` (default) basahin ``ports.internal.<proto>``; ``same`` Ginamit muli ang inilathalang daungan, para sa mga serbisyong hindi maaaring muling gamitin (SSTUN/TURN, media relays)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``internal``, container network only"
msgstr "``internal``, network ng container lamang"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` and ``mailroom`` are not deployed; ``gitlab.yml`` disables them."
msgstr "``kas`` (Kubernetes agent server, workspaces), ``pages``, ``registry`` at ``mailroom`` ay hindi ginagamit; ``gitlab.yml`` Pinipinsala sila."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_bits`` (int): RSA key size"
msgstr "``key_bits`` (int): RSA susing sukat"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key_host`` (string): host path to Root CA private key"
msgstr "``key_host`` (string): daan patungo sa Root CA pribadong susi"

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key`` names the pinned key and defaults to ``version``; an entity with several pins declares a list of such blocks. The types are ``git_tags`` (repository), ``registry_tags`` (image), ``npm`` (package), ``http_regex`` (url, pattern) and ``script`` (path, run with the current version and printing the latest one)."
msgstr "``key`` Sabihin ang pindutan na key at default ``version``; isang korporasyon na may iba't ibang tono ang nagpapahayag ng isang talaan ng gayong mga bloke. Ang mga uri ay ``git_tags`` (Pinaglalagyan), ``registry_tags`` (Larawan), ``npm`` (pakete), ``http_regex`` (Turl, parisan) at ``script`` (Path, run with the kasalukuyang bersyon at printing ang pinakabago)."

# translated-by: libretranslate
msgid "``key``: services.<key>.* lookup base. Default: provides or entity_name"
msgstr "``key``: serbisyo.<key>.* Pabalat ng paa. Default: nagbibigay o entity_name"

